{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/87","id":4895892650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVLzC488AAAABI9Fkqg","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/87","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/87.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/87.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/87","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/87/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/87/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/87/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/statuses/25cbffe6080bdf397f4911f85111cc966ac951d3","number":87,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"A05 Draft: native read-only HOS2 QueryAbi device in Asterinas","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## First genuine Asterinas-side HOS2 ioctl implementation candidate (read-only)\n\nThis is **A05 Draft**, not an assertion of G1. The current kernel still does **not** implement trusted CapSpace, process-start/exec-epoch lifecycle, ResourceDomain CAS, InstallBudget, ReadUsage, QueryDelivery, RetireThrough or Hepta durable effects.\n\n**Source:** independent branch `agents/A05-native-queryabi-bootstrap` at commit `5fc3887dfc5833b61d11280eb1421bb7fd78648f`, pinned base `8f3bb49ab161104063a6ebea25428c40aa884ac0`. Exactly 4 files; **README remains zero bytes**:\n- `kernel/asterinas/kernel/core/src/device/misc/hepta_control.rs`: restricted root-only devtmpfs char device `/dev/hepta-control` using Asterinas' existing char registry and `PerOpenFileOps::ioctl`; canonical HOS2 64-byte QueryAbi decode/112-byte response encoding via the **same** `libs/os-abi/src/lib.rs` source, not a second wire implementation. Allocates per-open temporary unique observation IDs, advertises **only** the QueryAbi operation. Invalid descriptor/request rejected without effect; all other ioctls ENOTTY.\n- `kernel/asterinas/kernel/core/src/{lib.rs,device/misc/mod.rs}`: minimal device registration and shared codec path.\n- `tests/kernel/control/queryabi_guest.c`: **compiled** statically linked x86_64 Linux ELF; checks actual ioctl response format, stable boot identity, per-open space-ID isolation, malformed magic EINVAL, NULL transport EFAULT, unknown ioctl ENOTTY.\n\n**Actual build evidence:** fixed upstream `nightly-2026-07-21` full `make kernel` compiled successfully using pinned Asterinas v0.19.0. Produced kernel ELF **SHA256 `54c8a7a798cbbd80f1a8ce5f0144328815e63b413e79b0133206bcaaba607e4a`**, size 8,352,152B. Guest C probe compiled with `cc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -static`. Build records are retained in authorized dev environment `/home/qian-qi/.local/state/trillionnium-os-organ-next-20261016/evidence/a05-native-queryabi-build-03/` and `-launch.log`.\n\n**Known build-environment issue:** main's pre-existing A01 `support/build/kernel.sh` invokes `make --version | head -1`/`gcc --version | head -1` under `set -o pipefail`; one attempt exited SIGPIPE 141 before compilation. For the successful private build only, replaced `head -1` with non-early-terminating `sed -n '1p'`; **reverted that A01-owned file before commit**. The PR changes no A01 build inputs or Cargo.lock.\n\n**Missing validation / genuine blockers:** an attempted custom QEMU QueryAbi guest runner and subsequent direct QEMU smoke were refused by the authorized execution channel. No successful kernel QueryAbi ioctl was executed; the C test is **compiled but not run as guest**. Full kernel boot from this particular new ELF, malformed kernel usercopy, fork/exec, authorization and production behavior all remain **NOT TESTED**. Do not mark G1 complete from compilation or from the Linux host QueryAbi/ENOTTY test.\n\n**Review instructions:** A05/A00 should next run the compiled guest probe in a disposable pinned one-vCPU QEMU initramfs, verify magic/version/op-mask/boot ID/fd ownership/error cases and measure copyout on EFAULT. Before considering main, replace the provisional per-open space ID with genuine trusted CapSpace session binding, publish a stable allocated ioctl number through A00, and use an explicit Cargo path dependency/lock arrangement for the canonical HOS2 crate if appropriate. This Draft adds *no effect authority*. Existing Hepta `TrustedReadOnlyOrganV1` remains I/O-free.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T00:37:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T01:00:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7246f7c39d41b0cc00054287814114ea038c431b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":